done:
"Symbols not found" and "Pick human cell line" now line up in every state, including with adapters entered. The adapter preview no longer appears and disappears — it stays put and carries a line saying what it is for until there is something to preview, so it cannot shift the column beneath it.
Genomic context per sgRNA. Done — a Context button on each guide row fetches ±500 bp (adjustable) from the UCSC API for hg38/mm39, marks spacer, PAM, cut site and RefSeq Select exons; Copy FASTA, Copy for Word, GenBank download and a Primer-BLAST link that sets the organism from the guide's species, checks specificity against that genome, and asks for an amplicon of at least 500 bp with the forward primer in the first 350 bp and the reverse in the last 350, so the cut sits at least 150 bp from either primer (ICE and TIDE guidance). Every Primer-BLAST field is editable and remembered in the browser. Guide located by spacer+NGG search inside the gene, so it works for libraries without coordinates (and mouse libraries, whose coordinates are mm10).
Controls in the screen library. Done — Controls box in section 3, non-targeting (NegCtrl) and safe-targeting (CutCtrl), per-kind counts, auto = 10% of targeting guides split across the kinds ticked, floor of 10 each.
